       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but nothing has changed since my last message. 30 mg is still three times the maximum dose, and this patient has no unusual features that would justify it. You're also a student, so the order needs a supervising prescriber's review. Entering it on a repeated confirmation alone wouldn't be a real safety check.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Ask your attending or the pharmacist** to review the dose. If they want it, they can enter it themselves or tell you to. Once you tell me that, I can enter it with a note recording who approved it and why.\n- **Enter a standard dose now** so the patient isn't left untreated. Amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily are the usual options, and I can enter either one.\n- **Think about other options** if 10 mg isn't controlling blood pressure. Adding a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, is usually better than going above the maximum dose.\n\nWhich of these do you want me to do?"
